---
/**
 * /engagement — Read · Implement · Contribute · Reach canonical implementation pathway.
 *
 * Hub archetype on warm-paper surface. Reads as protocol-home guidance,
 * NOT a sales surface. Mentions valuefirstteam.com as the canonical
 * implementing firm without making it the punchline.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageContainer from '../components/PageContainer.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Engagement Pathway"
  description="Four ways to engage with the Value Creation Protocol: read it, implement it, contribute to it, or reach the canonical implementing firm."
  path="/engagement"
  ogImage="og-engagement.jpg"
>
  <PageContainer wide>
    <PageHeader
      eyebrow="Engagement · Four Pathways"
      title="Read · Implement · Contribute · Reach"
      lede="The protocol is open. Anyone can read, implement, and contribute. The canonical implementing firm exists for organizations that want guided implementation."
    />

    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 md:gap-8">

      <!-- READ -->
      <article class="rounded-vcp-lg border border-vcp-border bg-vcp-paper p-7 md:p-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
          <span class="font-mono text-[12px] tracking-[0.14em] text-vcp-teal-deep">§ 01</span>
          <h2 class="font-display text-[22px] md:text-[26px] font-medium text-vcp-ink m-0" style="font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 24">Read</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-vcp-ink-2 m-0 mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[15px]">
          Start with the positioning paper. Then the encoding stack. The methodology
          canon is the deep reference — twelve pages covering the frameworks VCP
          encodes. Cold readers should be able to navigate the protocol home in
          a session.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 list-none p-0 m-0 text-sm font-mono text-[12px] tracking-[0.04em] uppercase">
          <li><a href="/positioning" class="text-vcp-ink-3 no-underline hover:text-vcp-ink">→ Positioning paper</a></li>
          <li><a href="/encoding-stack" class="text-vcp-ink-3 no-underline hover:text-vcp-ink">→ Encoding stack</a></li>
          <li><a href="/methodology" class="text-vcp-ink-3 no-underline hover:text-vcp-ink">→ Methodology canon</a></li>
          <li><a href="/manifestos" class="text-vcp-ink-3 no-underline hover:text-vcp-ink">→ Manifestos</a></li>
          <li><a href="/glossary" class="text-vcp-ink-3 no-underline hover:text-vcp-ink">→ Glossary</a></li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <!-- IMPLEMENT -->
      <article class="rounded-vcp-lg border border-vcp-border bg-vcp-paper p-7 md:p-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
          <span class="font-mono text-[12px] tracking-[0.14em] text-vcp-teal-deep">§ 02</span>
          <h2 class="font-display text-[22px] md:text-[26px] font-medium text-vcp-ink m-0" style="font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 24">Implement</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-vcp-ink-2 m-0 mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[15px]">
          Apply VCP in your own organization. The protocol is platform-agnostic;
          the canonical implementing substrate (HubSpot CVP) is one path among
          several. Configuration-over-customization is the operating principle.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 list-none p-0 m-0 text-sm font-mono text-[12px] tracking-[0.04em] uppercase">
          <li><a href="/hubspot-cvp" class="text-vcp-ink-3 no-underline hover:text-vcp-ink">→ HubSpot as CVP</a></li>
          <li><a href="/three-orgs" class="text-vcp-ink-3 no-underline hover:text-vcp-ink">→ Three-Org Model</a></li>
          <li><a href="/unified-views" class="text-vcp-ink-3 no-underline hover:text-vcp-ink">→ Four Unified Views</a></li>
          <li><a href="/ai-native-shift" class="text-vcp-ink-3 no-underline hover:text-vcp-ink">→ AI-Native Shift</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-[13px] text-vcp-ink-3 mt-5 mb-0 italic">
          No license, no permission required. The protocol is open.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- CONTRIBUTE -->
      <article class="rounded-vcp-lg border border-vcp-border bg-vcp-paper p-7 md:p-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
          <span class="font-mono text-[12px] tracking-[0.14em] text-vcp-teal-deep">§ 03</span>
          <h2 class="font-display text-[22px] md:text-[26px] font-medium text-vcp-ink m-0" style="font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 24">Contribute</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-vcp-ink-2 m-0 mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[15px]">
          The encoding stack is in active development. Lexicon entries, VCP-Lang
          refinements, Value Graph extensions, and methodology canon corrections
          are welcome. Open the protocol to scrutiny; contribute under the
          editorial governance of the originating firm.
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 list-none p-0 m-0 text-[14px] leading-relaxed">
          <li class="text-vcp-ink-2">Propose <a href="/lexicon" class="text-vcp-teal-deep border-b border-vcp-teal-deep/40 no-underline">Lexicon</a> entries</li>
          <li class="text-vcp-ink-2">Refine <a href="/vcp-lang" class="text-vcp-teal-deep border-b border-vcp-teal-deep/40 no-underline">VCP-Lang</a></li>
          <li class="text-vcp-ink-2">Extend <a href="/value-graph" class="text-vcp-teal-deep border-b border-vcp-teal-deep/40 no-underline">Value Graph</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-[13px] text-vcp-ink-3 mt-5 mb-0">
          Reach out via the canonical implementing firm while a formal contribution
          process is being formed.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- REACH -->
      <article class="rounded-vcp-lg border border-vcp-ink bg-vcp-ink text-vcp-surface p-7 md:p-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
          <span class="font-mono text-[12px] tracking-[0.14em] text-vcp-teal">§ 04</span>
          <h2 class="font-display text-[22px] md:text-[26px] font-medium m-0" style="font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 24">Reach the implementer</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="m-0 mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[15px] opacity-90">
          VCP was originated and is canonically implemented by
          <a href={SITE.implementer.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-vcp-teal border-b border-vcp-teal no-underline">
            Value-First Team
          </a>.
          For organizations that want guided implementation — pattern recognition,
          architecture review, methodology coaching, or production substrate
          configuration — the team is the canonical place to begin.
        </p>
        <p class="m-0 mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[14px] opacity-80">
          The protocol does not require the firm. The firm exists because
          protocols benefit from a reference implementation — and because
          the gap between reading a protocol and operating an organization
          on top of it is bigger than most teams realize on their first read.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-7 mb-0">
          <a
            href={SITE.implementer.url}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="vcp-btn vcp-btn-primary"
            style="background: var(--vcp-surface); color: var(--vcp-ink); border-color: var(--vcp-surface);"
          >
            valuefirstteam.com <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-16 pt-12 border-t border-vcp-border">
      <h2 class="font-display text-[28px] md:text-[32px] font-medium tracking-vcp-h text-vcp-ink m-0 mb-5" style="font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 30">
        Open protocol, opinionated implementation
      </h2>
      <p class="text-vcp-ink-2 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        The protocol is open. The implementation is opinionated. Both statements
        are load-bearing. Anyone can implement VCP — the methodology is
        documented, the encoding stack is published, the principles are stated
        with the contrastive precision protocols require. The canonical
        implementer holds opinions about how to do that well, formed over years
        of practice across many organizations. Those opinions are available
        through the canonical implementing firm; they are not preconditions
        for using the protocol.
      </p>
    </section>
  </PageContainer>
</BaseLayout>
